problems.problem:
Let $N$ be the set of natural numbers. Suppose $f : N \to N$ is a function satisfying the following conditions.
(a) $f(mn) = f(m)f(n)$;
(b) $f(m) < f(n)$ if $m < n$;
(c) $f(2) = 2$.
What is the value of $\displaystyle\sum_{k=1}^{20} f(k)$?

Find the number of triples $(a, b, c)$ of positive integers such that
(a) $ab$ is a prime;
(b) $bc$ is a product of two primes;
(c) $abc$ is not divisible by square of any prime and
(d) $abc \le 30$.
